# Fine-clump style of `crown-round` (#635, D162, author 2026-11-28: both styles are kept, some trees each): the round-3
# drawing the author saw in the playtest build, even rows of small lit leaf clumps; the same silhouette and limbs as
# `crown-round` (the big-mass style), so a tree can take either.
# Round crown (#635, D162; replaced the 96x40 `crown` of #421): the decor kind `crown-round-fine`, native 160x144, one
# frame, hung from the room top; its trunk stands under the frame's middle (trunk object x = crown x + 72). A tall rounded
# crown, deepest over the trunk, with one limb (trunk.grid's bark keys) leaving the trunk on the left into the lower leaves.
# Composed by copying hand-typed leaf and limb stamps. Palette: D120 leaf green (k 1b291b, d 202e20, m 233223, l 273627, olive tips n 2f301e),
# the bark keys; clumps lit from above (p 2e4030, o 35492f) and shadowed underneath (q 141f14); no ink, no violet.
# `leaves` (#593, D163): the wind's glints light the leaf keys m, l, n below row 8 (the rows above are over the floor camera's
# top edge); the lit tops p and o, the contour, the shades d and q and the bark stay dark (tools/wind_spots.py).
size 160 144
color q 141f14
color k 1b291b
color d 202e20
color m 233223
color l 273627
color n 2f301e
color p 2e4030
color o 35492f
color f 220e09
color b 2e1813
color c 39231d
color h 47302a
frame crown-round-fine
leaves 0 8 160 136
